{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807890Z","id":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","body":{"detail":"Stopping the daemon on exit hangs on AppLifecycleState.detached (runtime close, then supervisor.stop()), which is asynchronous; nothing holds the process open for it. Launching the debug app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory and stopping it with SIGTERM left the embedded clax (its PID from <support>/clax-home/daemon.json) running, and it had to be stopped by PID. DaemonSupervisor stops a daemon.json daemon whose /healthz answers with its PID before the next start (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart), so the next launch recovers; until then the daemon holds its port and CLAX_HOME. Whether Cmd-Q delivers detached in time is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"On macOS, answer applicationShouldTerminate with terminateLater in AppDelegate.swift, ask Dart over the native channel to stop the worker and the supervisor, then reply to the app.","summary":"A macOS quit or a killed app process can leave the daemon running until the next launch","tags":["needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807991Z","id":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":517},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"001e3f1ba895d304c889685fc43746a9bb0a245499e84ebeb16f0fbb08b565e5"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808034Z","id":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"c29baf4b0608cc6a7e82f93ce31e00e5cc00ff6782d89986a1a0a9cd96cfb96a"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T11:59:38.617363Z","id":"34743c995d3d880cd783eb65f75e319b0f37cbe1d2a1fd93803d73b53f0cd1a3","body":{"detail":"Failure: quit the macOS app the ordinary way (Cmd-Q, Clax > Quit, or the AppleScript quit event; closing the last window takes the same path through applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed). The app process exits and its clax child keeps running, reparented to launchd, holding its port and CLAX_HOME until the next launch kills it. Reproduced twice against a debug build of e51b5922 (flutter build macos --debug) launched with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory: osascript -e 'tell application \"<path>/clax_app.app\" to quit' ended the app (PIDs 1346 and 9232) and left clax (1970 and 9246) running with PPID 1; ps after five more seconds still listed it. The relaunch did stop 1970 through daemon.json, so the leak lasts until the next launch. The quit relies on AppLifecycleState.detached, whose handler starts an asynchronous runtime close and supervisor stop that nothing waits for. The osascript reply was error -128 (User canceled): FlutterAppDelegate answers applicationShouldTerminate with a cancel and hands the request to Dart as System.requestAppExit, so the framework's WidgetsBindingObserver.didRequestAppExit hook is called on this path and can hold the quit until the stop finishes.","kind":"blocker","references":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"Override didRequestAppExit in _AppRootState: await _runtime.close(), then await _s.supervisor.stop() (bounded by its SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL grace), then return AppExitResponse.exit. Test it with tester.binding.handleRequestAppExit() in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart, asserting the supervisor's stopCalls is 1 before the response is exit. Keep the detached path for Android.","summary":"Quitting the macOS app normally leaves the embedded daemon running","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.242908Z","id":"65e509cc146a8ee25f8c745eb40ad05efc1af12cd091430bd284341a6bbb51d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3b5c19c","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.243325Z","id":"9ec4b682111096624035b79e455173c94be72b34cda6dbc442c85f9ea80fd7e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3b5c19c","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"34743c995d3d880cd783eb65f75e319b0f37cbe1d2a1fd93803d73b53f0cd1a3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122975Z","id":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","body":{"detail":"The notification follows MakeStage labels for a make and a fixed 'Working on your comment' for a change. AgentLoop.newApp takes onProgress and the worker emits WorkerProgress (lib/agent/worker.dart:27), but neither is passed to BackgroundRuns.step yet; _onWorker ignores WorkerProgress. Wire a short text from them (for example the size of the page written so far) with _runs.step(run, text).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"e1f97f681e6e08136cf0804ce6d60450068f2a57662275f4abcab8db172f7354"},"summary":"The background notification's progress text is only the making stage; streamed progress is not shown","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.809488Z","id":"836ff72799bb4c958c710b34be6a3d99af195c465e62d7e400e8501f356c8fa0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: lib/app.dart steps the make's and each change's BackgroundRun with progressStep (the latest Narration or ToolStarted label) from newApp's onProgress and from WorkerProgress. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart: 'a make shows its narration and tools in the notification, then opens the app', 'a change shows its narration in the notification'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.814816Z","id":"1e60b9dd6740e8fa3af86895562b252ab0729fca6883ae81e18e815e7a0c9eb7","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e20425a31dc499f287202bd7fac1a475ffd1b2826f73351f3e21f112f08facf3"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","supersedes":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.815553Z","id":"16065304e8eab625b90a381011139ac6d8cef828f150ec11c0d1f44b6423a497","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":952},"content_hash":"fb1d2536c137cd71b52cfbfa3de58ed3c97d8aed3e107879ed4604d777f84c70"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","supersedes":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.819321Z","id":"7405e1efac450d08971f4c769b7924fcaab0f3508a491d21f05076ad3cbae48b","body":{"detail":"usesToolLoop (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) chooses the tool loop when an inspector is given and the settings' backend takes turns (MessagesApiBackend) or AppServices.runner is set (the debug build's ScriptedRunner from a {\"runs\": …} CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT file). Once U6 passes its WebViewInspector, the worker's and the making screen's runs go through toolLoopRunner (MessagesApiRunner over ResumingTurns on AppServices.clock) with FileAskedQuestions('<support>/asked.json') (already passed by lib/main.dart) and AppServices.readConsent for U6's consent dialog.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"8acffa2fbea63204d0f0c69a86ef326c14e84d1e0314b54002ed36dba2bd9103"},"summary":"For Task U6: the tool loop runs only with AppServices.inspector; lib/main.dart passes none yet, so every run of the running app still takes the single structured call","tags":["handoff","task:U6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.859954Z","id":"a649dc69ccefe6ffbb82d0603682eda2741ce0e9a2d7af8e3738b40ba60792df","body":{"detail":"AppRoot._aimed sends OpenThread once the shell's threads message lists the thread, which selects it in the page (its pin and card). The app screen's own thread page, with the reply and Retry, opens only from the panel (AppScreen._openThread in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart). An AppScreen parameter such as initialThread, opening ThreadDetail after the first ready, would land the person on the reply itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":941},"end":{"line":972},"content_hash":"068865621760b0d52560bb1f7d20da639591d7b4c95d77d451e888a569d0856e"},"summary":"An inbox reply opens its app and asks the shell to select the thread (claxHost.openThread); it does not open the app screen's thread page (ThreadDetail)","tags":["inbox","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.482928Z","id":"40a23bc6c371345de7f4ad75a5db71f470ab725dc7aeedf41b0caf1d294a5f78","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cc6ad3bd","summary":"Fixed: lib/main.dart passes a WebViewInspector (df3b2f45) and takes a {\"runs\"} script as the tool loop's runner (cc6ad3bd); AppRoot mounts InspectorHost and builds DialogReadConsent. Evidence: macOS debug build with CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT (str_replace, render, finish) on its real daemon took a sent thread to v2, thread resolved with the agent's reply, GET /api/drafts empty, agent-timings.jsonl {renders: 1, outcome: finished, turns: 3}; finish publishes only after a clean render (lib/agent/tools/finish.dart gate). flutter test: 1199 passed.","supersedes":"7405e1efac450d08971f4c769b7924fcaab0f3508a491d21f05076ad3cbae48b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:07:48.262640Z","id":"84335fdfd947a8ec5bbf90a00fa405959814636972c8cbb81afd0c614f61706a","body":{"detail":"The notice is cleared on the screen leaving the front (app_screen.dart _tellVisible), on quit, and in MainActivity.onDestroy, none of which runs when the process is killed or crashes while the screen is in front. AppRoot's initState does not clear it, so a cold launch from the launcher lands on the home screen with a stale 'Comment on it' notice. Tapping it still routes correctly (launchTap opens that app), so the harm is only a misleading notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":507},"content_hash":"33bde6b301a55679610acb66f82a16e825cca4a204740251e5d124b8b5229345"},"suggested_fix":"Clear the notice at AppRoot start unless launchTap returned a tap.","summary":"A notice left by a process that died while an app screen was in front stays in the shade after the next launch until an app screen replaces it","tags":["review","u7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:11:33.677572Z","id":"b71b30a4e3bfd6d5ea114b6d03fce208c09258e60fd654a19e52935410f68270","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:00f49272","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot.initState clears AppServices.notice before any app screen shows it. test/app_test.dart \"the notice's actions reach the app on top\" asserts the first call is clear and passes.","supersedes":"84335fdfd947a8ec5bbf90a00fa405959814636972c8cbb81afd0c614f61706a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:25:27.858754Z","id":"454e26ab3f8f097a141e8c9958b5d21f7014e0b60a1a0a21709284c8228c8159","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop.newApp (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:258) keeps the first run's plan under planKey (a fresh 'new:<micros>' when null) and moves it to the app's ID once it is made. AppRoot._make passes none, so nothing can watch PlanStore.watch(key) while the first run plans. The build view (task X1) should make a key starting with pendingPlanPrefix, pass it to newApp, watch it, then watch the app ID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":800},"end":{"line":806},"content_hash":"8a82c82e08bb71d42bbd1c8d4f11eb3e18c738d86f18186dc31efb31335206d6"},"summary":"The making screen cannot show the plan during a first run: _make does not pass a planKey to AgentLoop.newApp","tags":["handoff","task:X1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:53.200044Z","id":"484451658f03be85642fa5f357e8b5d7e773de4e990d4b1100d09e94a8d04723","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ae27f250","summary":"Fixed in ae27f250: AppRoot._make makes a pendingPlanPrefix key when the tool loop runs, reports it as MakePlanKey and passes it to AgentLoop.newApp; MakingScreen watches it, then the app's ID. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'shows the plan from the first run, offers Open app once the first version lands, and follows the build'. flutter test test/ui/build_view_test.dart: +8, all passed; flutter test test/ui test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +419, all passed.","supersedes":"454e26ab3f8f097a141e8c9958b5d21f7014e0b60a1a0a21709284c8228c8159","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.964543Z","id":"a7ecebe9d62f13cc8d8bc1154baaaa6fcacb2e3f1826f361349eccbe58ce9687","body":{"detail":"_onBuild calls _stepBuild for every BuildState, and the worker emits one per progress event of a continue run. Each call awaits PlanStore.get before BackgroundRuns.step, so two quick events can land in reverse order (an older step overwrites a newer one), and BackgroundRuns.step (platform/background_work.dart:248) dedupes only identical text, so every narration or tool start becomes a notification update. Android drops updates beyond its per-app rate, so the shown step can stick on a stale one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":999},"end":{"line":1020},"content_hash":"c7b762e186894e8ce1ad4a61bbe95ff428cea1471888f3143a582e1acf914f14"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the latest plan from PlanStore.watch per building app instead of a get per event, and throttle notification updates (for example at most one per second, always sending the last).","summary":"The build's notification is updated on every progress event, with a plan read from disk each time, unthrottled and possibly out of order","tags":["review","review:X1","build","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:05.964886Z","id":"e7ae4571902d1a6bff6cfe3fae5fab75a79764b83f22da9dfcfd335affdea095","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:418a9eff","summary":"Fixed in 9277b5e8 and 418a9eff: BuildNotices (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/build_notices.dart) shows a build's first state at once, then at most one update each second on the injected clock, the latest state winning, with the plan kept from PlanStore.watch rather than read per event. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_notices_test.dart. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"a7ecebe9d62f13cc8d8bc1154baaaa6fcacb2e3f1826f361349eccbe58ce9687","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082502Z","id":"0a2664b07c2795e61f202eed5501b7681ea10c839da055901930003cacd92cc0","body":{"detail":"_failedAway and _offerLostMake push the build view from AppRoot (_makingRoute) and do not read its MakingResult. Edit there cancels the make (MakeSession.cancel) and pops EditRequest, which only the launcher's _showMake (lib/ui/launcher.dart) turns into a New sheet holding the request. Opened from the failed tile instead, Edit works.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":936},"end":{"line":944},"content_hash":"4c89c433a99bbf27aba5b2506d1568a5fc2df439b7856d0ebb1d27fd365ff2f3"},"summary":"A build view opened from the failure toast or from Make it again ignores Edit: the request is dropped instead of reopening the New sheet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082564Z","id":"bb075ca4ceab5ecc1ee2d797aee15f3b5591da4e74675963a9dc6f0796b9342b","body":{"detail":"_made holds one app and Timings.start(sayUsable) is started by each make (_make), so a second Make restarts the clock and the first app's ready no longer stops it. The defended number is only right for one make at a time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":491},"content_hash":"a0e043f9428c26b727c270a80fcf4bb6d712869347b09d2a22becb698a8676c7"},"summary":"say-usable is one slot: with several makes at once it measures from the latest Make to whichever app that run made","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:10:51.019752Z","id":"e0550bb53be343e7d81137215d6b7f905f5bdc49f5a23b9d60028c8389fad7ff","body":{"detail":"_offerLostMake loops over PendingMake.takeAll and awaits a showDialog per request. With three makes cut off, the person answers three modal dialogs before reaching the launcher. One dialog listing the requests (with Make all / pick / Not now) or one making tile per lost request would ask once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":879},"end":{"line":907},"content_hash":"6cc8b9f705848e426ffd0a729d9b98ea98e35bb798047618b06078f0726400b8"},"summary":"Several lost makes at launch ask one 'Make it again?' dialog after another, and 'Not now' on any of them drops that request for good (takeAll deletes the file)","tags":["review","review:X2","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:16.755873Z","id":"4b6f863c0009849962ba7f815b60abe3a8b3d8dcff6bfa96ab4db48ac7441746","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:741f7d81","span":{"start":{"line":879},"end":{"line":907},"content_hash":"c67682eef1911b52161429ae8e4b160c8fc58748e27a465874f7ca373a21d2ad"},"summary":"Fixed: lost makes become Interrupted tiles (MakeService.lost), kept in PendingMake until Make it again or Discard; no launch dialogs. test/app_background_test.dart 'a make the last run never finished is an interrupted tile; Make it again runs it' and 'Discard forgets the lost make; closing the question keeps it' pass.","supersedes":"e0550bb53be343e7d81137215d6b7f905f5bdc49f5a23b9d60028c8389fad7ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:45:00.572970Z","id":"319800e5be58d3b471ecfacf2ff80938a43154f26b3127f289524373a92e5e83","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d4328753","summary":"Fixed: an inbox reply passes its comment ID (Launcher._openItem, 99b96744) and AppRoot._openTarget hands thread and comment to AppScreen.initialThread/initialComment (d4328753), which opens ThreadDetail at that comment once the page is first up (3e79f8d4). Tests pass: test/app_test.dart 'an inbox reply opens its app at the thread once the shell lists it, and its thread page at the reply; a version item at that version', test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'initialThread opens the thread page at its comment once the page is up', test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart 'a focused comment is scrolled to and lit, then fades'.","supersedes":"a649dc69ccefe6ffbb82d0603682eda2741ce0e9a2d7af8e3738b40ba60792df","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.923011Z","id":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","body":{"detail":"_presentQuestion adds the ID to _seenQuestions before choosing the background path. Returning to the question's own app still counts it in the change sheet (QuestionsMsg), and the inbox lists it; a launcher or making screen shows nothing until the notification is tapped. A fix: keep background questions in a pending set and present the newest still-open one on AppLifecycleState.resumed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1139},"end":{"line":1173},"content_hash":"ce7bb9deca3d335696cb1236b67af02133ddba62f7271f497b58fe7f93350f4a"},"summary":"A question that arrives while Clax is in the background is only posted as a notification: coming back without tapping it shows no sheet or toast, since the question is marked seen","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.923190Z","id":"7f28c8ffe91ef10b071c668d3d70c9b37fdf38b4c21bc3d298cceddad56d3ae3","body":{"detail":"The platform side (android/.../BackgroundRunService.kt Notices.news) treats the field as an opaque string extra and keys the notification ID by its hash, so it works without platform changes; but the convention lives only in app.dart. A typed BackgroundWork.question(title, text, qid) with its own tap stream would make it explicit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1122},"end":{"line":1122},"content_hash":"5cc6648706a4d640a900240ac3dfe82f3e35d3e215600e338488790bbbb9590e"},"summary":"A question notification rides on BackgroundWork.ready with the target 'question:<qid>' in its artifact field, which _onNews splits again","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:50.476383Z","id":"9757354add87a5bbc24d23b3bc5fa1c067670f0c9445ed1ad0a397161c39aa91","body":{"detail":"Failure: a session asks question A (no app, or with no app screen on top), the sheet opens on A; before A is answered the session (or another) asks B. B gets no sheet, toast or pending slot, and after A closes nothing shows B; it is found only in the inbox, while its asker waits (mode wait, then terminal after terminal_after_s). The same happens when the toast's View or an inbox tap names a question while the sheet shows another. A fix: keep a queue of open questions to present, and on the sheet's whenComplete open the next one still open (or switch the sheet to /inbox, which lists them all).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1175},"end":{"line":1193},"content_hash":"9a1d6b61539acaf98b64b3740aa43eb6a9d511d824118d451a94ac111ad515a3"},"summary":"A second question that lands while the question sheet shows one is dropped: _openQuestion returns on _sheetQuestion != null, and _onQuestionEvent has already marked it seen, so it is never presented","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:50.476583Z","id":"2f368b89d08f0eb1dc3ba731c8e6579078a403af1a523f7f396ccdd4fa8371db","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","summary":"On macOS this is total: lib/main.dart:155 gives macOS NoBackgroundWork, whose ready() does nothing (lib/platform/background_work.dart:58), so a question that lands while the window is hidden or minimised (AppLifecycleState.hidden, not foreground per lib/platform/network_pause.dart:29-32) posts no notification and is marked seen; coming back shows no sheet or toast. The fix proposed here (present the newest still-open background question on resume) covers both platforms.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.722222Z","id":"5dc944508ef244ccecacdb04cb3ae3efc6936b0af4d3ba9491af3ae006fc2bc4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9a85457c","summary":"Fixed in 9a85457c: _showQuestion queues a question while the sheet shows another (or before the daemon is up), and the sheet's whenComplete runs _nextQuestion, skipping questions closed meanwhile. Evidence: test/app_test.dart 'questions asked while the sheet shows one wait for it to close; one answered meanwhile is skipped' (4376166f); flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: All tests passed (+49).","supersedes":"9757354add87a5bbc24d23b3bc5fa1c067670f0c9445ed1ad0a397161c39aa91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.723512Z","id":"8818cc1a6ecb4b92efd81d6926c4b06d1238d884072e3eaf6a11c6012216ffe8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9a85457c","summary":"Fixed in 9a85457c: a question posted in the background is kept in _backgroundQuestions and presented through _presentQuestion when AppPresence says foreground again (any platform, so macOS hidden/minimised too): the sheet over Clax's screens, a toast over another app, nothing over its own app; one closed meanwhile is skipped. Evidence: test/app_background_test.dart 'coming back without tapping the notification shows a question still open in the sheet…' and 'a background question about another app is told in a toast on return…' (4376166f), both failing on the previous app.dart; flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: All tests passed (+49).","supersedes":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.724675Z","id":"044caf34289a4ef5c49b4884b281f8694755c8cdd407ab2d55478b15f88ccbca","body":{"detail":"_presentQuestion shows a toast with hideCurrentSnackBar for each question not about the app on top, and toasts do not take a sheet slot, so _presentBackgroundQuestions and _nextQuestion present them back to back. The others stay in the inbox and the change sheet's question count. A fix: one toast 'Clax has N questions' whose View opens the first and queues the rest.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1158},"end":{"line":1164},"content_hash":"5bb7ef30fb9a35695f6e3039e5f31b557c8932dd857a696bd32c2dd7c8932eca"},"summary":"Several background questions about other apps, presented on return over an app, each replace the previous toast: only the last one's View shows","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:17.325899Z","id":"e5c1eb520c027cabdf6f014f3bfe0dd9c224f9380787f91d6fac4bc35486bfdc","body":{"detail":"The daemon withdraws hook questions at start (crates/clax-core/src/store/questions.rs:827 withdraw_hook_questions_on_start) before the app's stream resubscribes, and SharedClaxStream reports the gap only as a `resync` event (lib/clax/shared_stream.dart:134), which _onQuestionEvent drops. _questionQueue and _backgroundQuestions survive Failed/Up, and _nextQuestion (scheduled on Up) and _presentBackgroundQuestions trust _openQuestions, so a withdrawn question opens the sheet unprompted. A fix: on a questions resync, refetch the open questions and drop the rest from _openQuestions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1137},"end":{"line":1154},"content_hash":"341d61e14338a1beaa6ea3ae0d15d5f0ea557c6954c5e47e357105857960844f"},"summary":"_openQuestions ignores the questions topic's resync, so after a daemon restart a queued or background question the daemon withdrew is still presented in the sheet","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:17.326083Z","id":"b5c2b7f2d8ffed40e020ea8b318546d07033e841fee98a6559942333ba62e015","body":{"detail":"On Android the return to the foreground (inactive) reaches didChangeAppLifecycleState before the tap reaches _onNews. With background questions A and B open and B's notification tapped, _presentBackgroundQuestions opens the sheet on A and queues B (asked: false); the tap's _openQuestion(B) upgrades the queued entry to asked and moves it to the end, so the person sees A until they close it. A fix: an asked question goes to the front of the queue, or replaces a sheet opened by _presentBackgroundQuestions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1209},"end":{"line":1221},"content_hash":"d323815a2b01755ea38bccd4ee8864faca3ce17bbe1dcf84f0d5c395b019fab3"},"summary":"A tapped question notification can show a different question first: coming back presents the oldest background question in the sheet, and the tap's question is queued behind it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:52.464807Z","id":"3400659a9be6175bfa618ea306ef4bd7f8a2ca20537668d28043307d80781caf","body":{"detail":"WebViewAppSurface sets the key cookie before each load and reload (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart _setKey). WebViewQuestionPage (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart) has no such hook: it relies on the cookie this listener puts in the shared WebView cookie store on each Up, which is asynchronous, so a load that starts before setCookie completes is answered 401. After a daemon restart (new token, same port) an open shell's token, owner and events cookies are stale: its requests are 401 until the shell asks /api/token again with the new key cookie, or the page reloads. Checked on macOS for WebViewAppSurface only (apps/clax_app/integration_test/locked_daemon_test.dart); the question page and Android are unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"3bf62e9b3cfc04c844c500d4d6474bf874c0244672c552c6fc7e71ec6aba392b"},"summary":"WebViews other than WebViewAppSurface get the key cookie only from the Up listener, and an open shell is not reloaded after a restart","tags":["security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:12:27.615216Z","id":"66663ece3e306bea67d919ccb0e36499641bf13fdce664ad21cc8b65a19cb923","body":{"detail":"Failure: any new app made on the tool loop (an inspector, a Messages API or scripted runner) whose making screen hands over with a last render (_handOver passes lastFrame as the cover). _AppPageState.build returns Stack([screen, made-cover]) while _cover is set and the bare screen once the shell's Ready uncovers it; the screen changes parent, so its AppScreen element is unmounted and mounted again: the first AppScreenState's dispose calls widget.surface.dispose(), and the new one starts with _covered = true and never sees a Ready (the shell already sent it). Seen in apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop_test.dart (macOS, real daemon and WebViewInspector): the rig's listener got Ready for v1, 'made-cover' was gone and 'app-cover' (the spinner) stayed, so the two-finger swipe never reached the page (log target/flutter-app/i1-tool.log). The single-call path (full_loop_test.dart) hands over without a cover and does not hit it. test/app_background_test.dart checks only that 'made-cover' goes, not that the page is uncovered.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1601},"end":{"line":1624},"content_hash":"16dba17a1439da31f2468506b078b480b62f83420c1edfacc523a3e11e547295"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the tree shape fixed: always return Stack(fit: StackFit.expand, children: [screen, if (cover != null) ColoredBox(...)]) (or give the screen a GlobalKey), and in app_background_test.dart's hand-over test expect find.byKey(ValueKey('app-cover')) to find nothing after the Ready.","summary":"A tool-loop make handed over with its last render as the cover leaves the app screen covered by its spinner for good","tags":["review","integration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:50.990979Z","id":"21772190327e7790a29301055ffe379a275c0fed36f61ef2e76aa897e64d58b6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb389da","summary":"Fixed: _AppPage builds the same Stack with or without the made-cover, so the Ready that removes it keeps the AppScreen. test/app_background_test.dart 'a make streams to the making screen, which hands over to the new app in its place, covered by the last render until ready' now checks the same AppScreen State survives, its surface is not disposed and no app-cover remains; it failed before the fix (line 769) and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"66663ece3e306bea67d919ccb0e36499641bf13fdce664ad21cc8b65a19cb923","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.020832Z","id":"efc484e44388ed28396945cb9aa0db0ffd575da785a126176f8a0eaf083c548b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f3f9bf99","summary":"Fixed: a questions resync, Up with a queue and the return to the foreground recheck open questions with ClaxApi.questions (_recheckQuestions) and drop the ones no longer open. Tests (failed before f3f9bf99, pass after; flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed): app_test.dart 'a queued question the daemon withdrew without a stream event is dropped on the questions resync', 'after a daemon restart a queued question it withdrew is not shown'; app_background_test.dart 'a background question the daemon withdrew without a stream event is not shown on return'.","supersedes":"e5c1eb520c027cabdf6f014f3bfe0dd9c224f9380787f91d6fac4bc35486bfdc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.050415Z","id":"2b1abe1d3fc86ce98015a5c5c0025bafe34901d30d74fa49e912ceb7a0427a6e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f3f9bf99","summary":"Fixed: an asked question queues ahead of new ones and takes the place of a sheet showing an unasked one, which goes back to the queue behind it; background presentation also waits for the recheck. app_background_test.dart 'a tapped question notification shows its question first, the other background question after it' failed before (showed A) and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"b5c2b7f2d8ffed40e020ea8b318546d07033e841fee98a6559942333ba62e015","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.080438Z","id":"0ae4eb4adcfa226e1c2c82a7e3c55679fe46ea2234a24406b30f658eb15f8788","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f3f9bf99","summary":"Fixed: _presentQuestions tells all questions about other apps over an app in one toast ('Clax has N questions' when several), whose View opens each in turn; _nextQuestion gathers them too. app_background_test.dart 'several background questions about other apps are told in one toast on return; its View shows each in turn' failed before and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"044caf34289a4ef5c49b4884b281f8694755c8cdd407ab2d55478b15f88ccbca","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:22:33.326750Z","id":"ff4575c41b4112330d0cea4454a26e151fc9fe7ab091aa0c8d92eaf9d0f0f915","body":{"detail":"The removal loop runs over _openQuestions as it is when the response lands, not as it was when the request went out. A question event handled during the await (e.g. one asked just after a questions resync, or just after the daemon comes up in _recheckThenNext) is absent from the older snapshot, so it is removed from _openQuestions and _backgroundQuestions and added to _seenQuestions. If it was queued behind a showing sheet, _nextQuestion (app.dart:1366-1367) then skips it; a tapped notification for it is skipped too (seen, no view). The inbox still lists it. A live close cannot be undone by the recheck (it only removes), so answers are safe.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1174},"end":{"line":1188},"content_hash":"00e55b5d8d8858fa6dcd646ade1b41e7358186faaa6f175d71f453a326b537e2"},"suggested_fix":"Snapshot [..._openQuestions.keys] before the await and only drop IDs from that snapshot that the response lacks.","summary":"_recheckQuestions drops a question that arrives on the stream while its questions() request is in flight, so a queued or background question can be lost","tags":["review","N2c","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:22:33.326902Z","id":"cd7c2dac4b3dd02b0513fb7a6a30c0adf260f63ef4ac12c9945594f3ececdd5b","body":{"detail":"test/app_background_test.dart's tapped-notification test opens the asked question before the recheck queues the other, so the sheet it replaces is never showing; no test in test/app_test.dart or test/app_background_test.dart reaches removeRoute. By reading, the path is sound on the installed SDK: NavigatorState.removeRoute completes the route's future (navigator.dart:5733-5751, entry.complete), so whenComplete clears _sheetQuestion/_sheetRoute and shows the asked one, and a second asked question in the same window is queued without a second removeRoute (route.isActive is false). A regression here would leave a stuck _sheetQuestion and no further sheets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1302},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"428f44233f73c4f3db86016370b266794031ce5532b86d32d5efbee76bb90ede"},"suggested_fix":"A test in test/app_test.dart: a question about no app shows its sheet unasked, then the inbox opens a second; expect the second loaded, and after Close the first again.","summary":"The path where an asked question takes the place of an unasked sheet (removeRoute, then the old completion shows the asked one) has no test","tags":["review","N2c","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:24:37.100739Z","id":"f43a24cfafb8587e7d544f8488a808c92e5e5689f48448a7a4578dc9332d173e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:66b64c87","summary":"Fixed in 66b64c87: _recheckQuestions copies the open question keys before the await and drops only those. d4c73f7d adds 'a question that lands while the recheck is in flight is kept' (FakeClaxApi.holdQuestions holds the answer while a second question lands); it failed before the fix (QuestionWebSheet not found after closing the first) and passes now. flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +55, All tests passed.","supersedes":"ff4575c41b4112330d0cea4454a26e151fc9fe7ab091aa0c8d92eaf9d0f0f915","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.959670Z","id":"15f3b01f6c903f2caaeb5b3a3bc3573ef55371a0e2920b53507fbe555b33d13a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:478e81c2","summary":"Every daemon WebView loads through CookieLoads (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart), which awaits DaemonKeyCookie.ready before each load and reload: WebViewAppSurface (shell and inspector) and WebViewQuestionPage, which main.dart now passes to AppServices.questionPage. On a restart, main.dart's Up listener calls DaemonKeyCookie.refresh; a new token's cookie is set first, then restarts fires and a loaded question page reloads (followRestarts). An open app page already reloads on the endpoint's new PID (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _AppPageState._onEndpoint), through the same awaited cookie. flutter test test/ui/daemon_cookie_test.dart: 6 passed (load and reload wait for a cookie write held open by the test; a loaded page following restarts reloads after the new cookie is set; an unloaded or disposed page does not). A real WebView run on Android stays open on 18cb7cff.","supersedes":"3400659a9be6175bfa618ea306ef4bd7f8a2ca20537668d28043307d80781caf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:17:45.428307Z","id":"c8e36cbdd1773918755742af1ce5885ee80428176554a939988c804eef387a7d","body":{"detail":"test/app_bundles_test.dart covers a file opened before the daemon is up, a refusal and forgetDeleted. Nothing tests that _recoverBundles shows one BundleNoticeSheet per RecoveredUpdate and the 'Shared apps' damaged notice exactly once (only _bundlesStarted guards them), that two files opened together show their sheets one after another through _bundleQueue, or that delete is false off Android (line 796): flutter test runs as android, so the macOS branch that must never delete the person's own file has no test. A sheet dropped because _nav.currentContext is null (line 763) also leaves Android's cache copy undeleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":774},"end":{"line":845},"content_hash":"60cf79913f56f65c23568a53ee22cff2c487e1a3f5e808694c402dce092e8b35"},"suggested_fix":"App tests with debugDefaultTargetPlatformOverride = TargetPlatform.macOS asserting the opened file still exists; a pre-written snapshot under supportDir/snapshots and an unreadable lineage file, asserting each notice once across a daemon restart; two FakeBundleIntake.open calls in a row.","summary":"The start-up bundle wiring's notices and platform rule are untested: recoverInterrupted's notices, the damaged-lineage notice, several queued files, and macOS keeping the opened file","tags":["bundles","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928336Z","id":"6833bf1756e0ebca997dc05c4de5f78f1d527e5a1b75694e14d7abc72938c3fb","body":{"detail":"HomeHost.summaries leaves out only settings.homeAppId (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart). Installer.install (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart) creates the artifact, writes its lineage entry, seeds documents and keeps the bundle before it returns the ID, and the Launcher behind HomeRoute redraws on the gallery event in between. Seen only in the fallback grid, until the home app's first ready replaces it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":881},"end":{"line":898},"content_hash":"c93628b91fdcdb1e4dadae78f1d415ea78f45fad9e5b684b13215cd12e9cd4b2"},"summary":"On the first run the built-in home screen can list the home app's own tile ('Home') for a moment: the installer's createArtifact fires a gallery version event before ensureHomeApp saves homeAppId and settingsChanged hides it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
